SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast A Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Cast A (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 7:30 PM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 7:15 PM.\nOn stage: 8:10 PM–8:50 PM.\nACT II
  Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nMANDATORY — p
 roduction week.\n\n*** STANDING RULES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time dan
 cers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Ti
 me.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgi
 ving and Production Week Rehearsals and Performances).\nAll Casts are ca
 lled unless a cast is named.\nSUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedu
 le\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal are the official source. Mas
 ter: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-
 N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP — Tea ***\nChinese Te
 a — Costume (you provide): Pink Seamless Tights\, Flesh-tone camisole 
 leotard\; Shoes: Pink Pointe Shoes w/ ribbons & elastics (clean\, quiet\
 , unpancacked)\; Makeup: Full Stage Makeup - Mascara Only OK\; Hair: Hig
 h Bun\, No Part\nFull Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n• Apply foundat
 ion and powder matching skintone\n• Light skin tone eye shadow over en
 tire eye\n• Dark brown eye shadow over crease\n• Medium brown eye sh
 adow blended over brown\n• Black fake eyelashes (note: apply mascara t
 o own lashes before application of fake lashes)\n• Apply eyeliner afte
 r lashes dry\n• Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer
  doesn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n• Brown or tan on con
 tour cheekbones\, hairline\n• Use a brow pencil (or eyeshadow) to dark
 en the eyebrows\n• Red or Dark Red Lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear
  flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines
 :\n• Handle costume pieces with care while changing to prevent damage 
 to delicate fabrics\n• Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of
  costume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how significant\n
 • Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang costumes 
 by their elastic straps\n• Refrain from sitting on the floor while in 
 costume\n• Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any cos
 tume or accessory\n• Never apply stage make-up while in costume and sh
 all take great care to refrain from smudging make-up on costume during i
 ts removal\n• Refrain from the use of spray perfume or cologne while i
 n costume\n• Never wear any garment not assigned to cast member\n• D
 o not handle or consume food or beverage while in costume\, with the exc
 eption of water\n• Do not remove costumes from their assigned dressing
  rooms or from the theater\n• Remove all bobby pins used to secure hea
 d pieces and wigs following their use\n• Return all headpieces to thei
 r assigned bags\n• Comply fully with any and all updates to Ballet Ark
 ansas’ wardrobe policies\n• Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored d
 rinks or anything that may damage or stain costumes.
