SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast A @ 7:30PM – ACT II Cast A (Mandatory – Prod
 uction Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 7:45 PM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 7:30 PM.\nOn stage: 8:30 PM–9:20 PM.\nACT II
  Cast A Performance.\nMANDATORY — production week.\n\n*** STANDING RUL
 ES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time dancers should be check-in and backsta
 ge - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Time.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st 
 Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgiving and Production Week Rehearsals
  and Performances).\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named.\nSUBJE
 CT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and the B
 A portal are the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/spread
 sheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / 
 HAIR / MAKEUP — Tea ***\nChinese Tea — Costume (you provide): Pink S
 eamless Tights\, Flesh-tone camisole leotard\; Shoes: Pink Pointe Shoes 
 w/ ribbons & elastics (clean\, quiet\, unpancacked)\; Makeup: Full Stage
  Makeup - Mascara Only OK\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\nFull Stage Makeup 
 Instruction Sheet:\n• Apply foundation and powder matching skintone\n
 • Light skin tone eye shadow over entire eye\n• Dark brown eye shado
 w over crease\n• Medium brown eye shadow blended over brown\n• Black
  fake eyelashes (note: apply mascara to own lashes before application of
  fake lashes)\n• Apply eyeliner after lashes dry\n• Blush on the che
 eks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the 
 stage lights)\n• Brown or tan on contour cheekbones\, hairline\n• Us
 e a brow pencil (or eyeshadow) to darken the eyebrows\n• Red or Dark R
 ed Lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone 
 ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n• Handle costume pieces with 
 care while changing to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n• Promptly 
 notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume damage at the point of di
 scovery\, no matter how significant\n• Never throw costumes or accesso
 ries on the floor\, or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n• Refrai
 n from sitting on the floor while in costume\n• Do not attempt to alte
 r\, mend\, clean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n• Never apply 
 stage make-up while in costume and shall take great care to refrain from
  smudging make-up on costume during its removal\n• Refrain from the us
 e of spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n• Never wear any garme
 nt not assigned to cast member\n• Do not handle or consume food or bev
 erage while in costume\, with the exception of water\n• Do not remove 
 costumes from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n• Rem
 ove all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following their u
 se\n• Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n• Comply fully w
 ith any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n• Do 
 not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may damage o
 r stain costumes.
